# Static analysis configuration.
#
# The selection targets the bug classes that actually occur in this codebase:
# null dereferences, unchecked returns, and width or sign changes on lengths.
# Checks that fight C idioms, or that only make sense for C++, are off.
#
# Disabled deliberately:
#   readability-uppercase-literal-suffix  this codebase writes lowercase `u`
#                                         throughout, which is the prevailing
#                                         C convention; consistency is the
#                                         property that matters and it has it
#   misc-include-cleaner                  wants every transitively-used symbol
#                                         to have a direct include, which for
#                                         C means listing <stddef.h> beside
#                                         every header that already provides
#                                         size_t
#   readability-implicit-bool-conversion  `if (ptr)` and `if (len)` are C
#   *-magic-numbers, identifier-length    protocol constants and short loop
#                                         variables are not defects
#   *.DeprecatedOrUnsafeBufferHandling     wants memset_s/memcpy_s. Those are
#                                         C11 Annex K, which is OPTIONAL and
#                                         which neither glibc nor Apple's libc
#                                         implements -- taking the advice would
#                                         not compile on either platform this
#                                         library targets. Every length here
#                                         already goes through the checked
#                                         arithmetic in tamga_mem.h, which is
#                                         the property the check is reaching
#                                         for. It fires on Linux and not on
#                                         macOS, which is how it stayed
#                                         invisible until the first Linux run.
Checks: >
  clang-analyzer-*,
  bugprone-*,
  cert-*,
  misc-*,
  performance-*,
  readability-*,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -readability-identifier-length,
  -readability-magic-numbers,
  -readability-function-cognitive-complexity,
  -readability-braces-around-statements,
  -readability-isolate-declaration,
  -readability-uppercase-literal-suffix,
  -readability-implicit-bool-conversion,
  -readability-use-concise-preprocessor-directives,
  -misc-no-recursion,
  -misc-include-cleaner,
  -cert-err33-c,
  -clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.DeprecatedOrUnsafeBufferHandling

WarningsAsErrors: 'clang-analyzer-*,bugprone-*'
HeaderFilterRegex: '^.*/(src|include)/.*'
FormatStyle: file
